<title>USA: Raytheon has no comment on Hughes bid.</title>
<headline>Raytheon has no comment on Hughes bid.</headline>
<dateline>BOSTON 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Raytheon Co declined comment Thursday on a published report that it had offered $9 billion for the defense assets of Hughes Electronics Corp.</p>
<p>&quot;We have no comment on that,&quot; Raytheon spokesman Robert McWade said of the Wall Street Journal report. &quot;We just don't comment on the specualtion or information people get from their sources.&quot;</p>
<p>The newspaper, quoting &quot;people familiar with the developments,&quot; said Northrop Grumman Corp had offered even more than Raytheon for Hughes -- $200-$500 million more.</p>
<p>Hughes is a unit of General Motors Corp.</p>
<p>GM will accept equity as partial payment for Hughes, and the winning bidder will have to assume debt, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>((-- Boston Bureau (617) 367-4106))</p>
</text>
